# Nothing in this directory is ever served over the web.
#
# On doc.infodot.co.za the application lives INSIDE the web root: the
# domain's document root is this directory's parent, and a hand-written
# index.php there boots the app from here (see .ai/rules/deploy.md). Without
# this file every plain file under it is a public URL - confirmed live:
# /doc/database/database.sqlite (the whole database) and
# /doc/storage/logs/laravel.log were both downloadable by anyone.
#
# PHP's require/include read the filesystem, not the web, so the app itself
# is unaffected. On a conventional layout (document root = public/) this
# file sits outside the web root and does nothing.
#
# Both forms on purpose: `Require` is the access rule, and the rewrite is a
# second lock that does not depend on which access module the server honours.
Require all denied

RewriteEngine On
RewriteRule ^ - [F,L]
